-(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults.) Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, and AWAITING-APPROVAL sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
+(`MISSING` and `MALFORMED` sit outside this derivation — they are registration and contract faults.) One park layers onto READY: a set that declared the **Explore directive**, has no **Exploration report**, and whose **Explore phase** gave up reads EXPLORE-FAILED — derived from its latest **Captured run** of phase `explore` plus the absent report, with no stored column (ADR-0262). Automatic selection runs READY sets in scheduler order and passes over DONE, DEFERRED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, and EXPLORE-FAILED sets; only when no READY set exists may a no-argument implement select a single unambiguous Human-blocked Task set for attended help, and only when the block is an open HITL task rather than an unresolved AFK dependency. Multiple Human-blocked Task sets are ambiguous and require an explicit target. Draining stops when its selected set reaches DONE, FAILED, BLOCKED, AWAITING-APPROVAL, VERIFY-FAILED, EXPLORE-FAILED, or DEFERRED, or when an **Agent quota pause** interrupts draining without changing task status. At a BLOCKED HITL gate, interactive runs show a **HITL gate prompt** while non-interactive runs and `--yes` preserve stop-and-advice output and never auto-start attended assistance.
 
 **Tasks readiness**:
 The **Doctor status** of the `pop tasks` command family. Because the tasks feature is aimed at Git projects and its central workflow is agent execution from a **Runtime path**, Doctor reports `pop tasks` as Blocked when no Git runtime checkout can be resolved, even if read-only status rendering could still inspect local artifacts.
@@ -770,6 +770,22 @@ _Avoid_: Reviewer, polisher, fixer, critic, linter
 Formerly the Review artifact. The single living document **Refine** maintains for a **Task set**: what the latest pass fixed, the smells it left, and the SHA of the tree it describes. Each pass supersedes rather than appends — the **Refiner** reads the previous report and writes the current one, carrying forward what is still true; prior documents stay under the set's directory and every reader takes the latest by timestamp. A **Task artifact**, so it never enters an **Implementation commit**; reaching a PR is an explicit human act. Humans meet it as a pointer at the **HITL gate prompt** and in the **Task set detail view**, and an **Assist session**'s prompt names its path.
 _Avoid_: Review artifact, review report, findings file, smell list
 
+**Exploration report**:
+The **Task set**'s third flat artifact, `exploration.md` beside the spec and the **Progress record** — what was decided, what exists, what happened. It records the code as found in the area the set's tasks touch: where things live, which seam owns what, which invariants hold, the test shape, and which files to read in ranges, every claim naming a path or a symbol, on about a page, stating as prose the tree it was observed at. Written once by the **Explore phase** and rewritten in place by `pop tasks explore`; no directory of timestamped documents, because nothing reruns it to supersede. Every implement attempt is handed its path, never its body, with one correction duty: a builder edits it only to fix a line its own attempt falsified. Nothing compares its recorded tree to the checkout — absent means write it, present means reuse it. It carries no prior-art section.
+_Avoid_: exploration notes, codebase map, journal, scratch pad
+
+**Explore phase**:
+The **Drain** step that writes the **Exploration report**, at the head of the drain before the first task is selected, for a set that declared the **Explore directive** and has no report. A fresh **Explorer** — the one role spawned under the **Read-only agent posture** — is given the set's manifest listing, task bodies and spec. Gated by `[work.explore].enabled`, which defaults **on**: the first agent phase that runs unasked, safe because only a set's own directive triggers it. It gates: a pass that gives up after the standard per-phase retry cap parks the set at EXPLORE-FAILED and appends one set-level **Progress record** naming the phase and the reason. Its runs are **Captured run**s of phase `explore`, and it spends against a **Spent retry cap** of its own. A **Human completion** is skipped. Three doors leave the park: `pop tasks explore <set>` (runs on any set, whatever its directive says), `pop tasks implement <set> --skip-explore` (drains once, unexplored and unparked), and `"explore": false`.
+_Avoid_: exploration step, pre-flight, survey
+
+**Explore directive**:
+The set-level `"explore": true` manifest key: the set's author declaring that two or more AFK tasks touch the same seam and a later one depends on how an earlier one shapes it. Opt-**in**, where `verify` and `refine` are opt-out — absent or false means the set never explores. It sits outside the **Agent directive** family, whose members only steer; its steering twin is the optional `"explorer": {"agents", "effort"}` object.
+_Avoid_: explore flag, needs-exploration
+
+**Explore mark**:
+Whether a set that declared the **Explore directive** got its **Exploration report** — `explored` or `unexplored` — carried beside its status like the **Verification mark**, with the reason (not yet run, or the pass failed) as detail beside it rather than a value inside it. A set that never declared carries none. Resolved once per refresh and read by every surface: the **Work dashboard** row and detail view, `pop work status`, `pop tasks status`, and the HITL sign-off gate, which names the report as a pointer (path plus recorded tree) beside the **Refine report**.
+_Avoid_: explore status, exploration badge
+
 **Refine episode**:
 Formerly the Review episode, with one carve-out: it ends only when the set's done-AFK composition changes through *non-remediation* work. A **Remediation task**'s completion never re-arms automatic **Refine**, so a verify-remediation lap re-verifies without re-refining — the heavy pass stays out of exactly the iteration that should be cheapest — at the accepted cost that a remediation diff lands unrefined until the next real work re-arms the episode. Manual `pop tasks refine` runs at any time regardless.
 _Avoid_: Review episode, refine cycle, refine generation
@@ -1237,7 +1253,7 @@ _Avoid_: Done Task set, Human-blocked Task set
 The governed move of one task between the four statuses (open, done, failed, skipped) through a single chokepoint. Legality is keyed by (from, to, actor): the **Task executor** may drive only open→done and open→failed; the human — via **Complete task**, **Skip**, and **Open task** — drives open→done (clearing a HITL task is this edge), failed→open, failed→done, open→skipped, skipped→open, skipped→done, and done→open. Every transition appends a **Progress record**, maintains the recorded attempt count (set on entering failed, cleared otherwise), lands as one atomic manifest write per batch, and applies **Verification invalidation** per its trigger rule. No other writer may change a task's status.
 
 **Progress record**:
-The append-only local `progress.txt` history beside a task manifest. It records terminal Done and Failed outcomes, explicit task reopenings, and manual completions. Intermediate attempts are streamed during execution but are not appended.
+The append-only local `progress.txt` history beside a task manifest. It records terminal Done and Failed outcomes, explicit task reopenings, manual completions, and set-level events such as an **Explore phase** park. Intermediate attempts are streamed during execution but are not appended.
 _Avoid_: Task state, agent output log
 
